      "sourceTextSha256": "34fd788fef0c717c8b520280e9c14284d2889f76bd5d9e80d0e6de487b86dc72",
      "text": "Breakfast, then board the Vistadome train through the Sacred Valley, along the roaring, rock-strewn Urubamba River, to the small town of Aguas Calientes; a 30-minute bus ride takes you up to Machu Picchu.\n\nWith its labyrinth of finely crafted stone temples, houses and fountains, the Inca citadel sits on a ridge between two mountain peaks. Long hidden beneath dense vegetation, it was brought to international attention by Hiram Bingham in 1911. Guided tour, lunch in the afternoon and return to Cusco by train. Transfer to the hotel.",
